  "dom_id": "step-q60313",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/a0101946d5e26e7296d91feb5b16b677e7ad0fb233b18812a653e32beee1e831.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?",
  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{5}{6}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{2}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $2$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/b7272117a60f88b4db5d6ee7e6d2ab0ddbce5fc1ae4646bbbd4eef0044145765.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{10}{18}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/c374b0f1ec8efd185b9067a8b48a2d88544b3ac543c177c5818451294d6af680.png)",
